---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretChangeResult = await interpretChange(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const resolveApplicabilityResult = await resolveApplicability(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretChangeResult.accepted);
const traceDependenciesResult = await traceDependencies(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, resolveApplicabilityResult.accepted);
const planImplementationResult = await planImplementation(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, traceDependenciesResult.accepted);
const verifyConfigurationResult = await verifyConfiguration(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planImplementationResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretChange: interpretChangeResult, resolveApplicability: resolveApplicabilityResult, traceDependencies: traceDependenciesResult, planImplementation: planImplementationResult, verifyConfiguration: verifyConfigurationResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretChangeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...resolveApplicabilityResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...traceDependenciesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planImplementationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyConfigurationResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretChangeResult.checks, ...resolveApplicabilityResult.checks, ...traceDependenciesResult.checks, ...planImplementationResult.checks, ...verifyConfigurationResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — Old and new parts coexist in inventory: enforce configuration-specific selection rather than blanket replacement. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (enforce configuration-specific selection rather than blanket replacement.) through the existing stage result for DesignDelta; preserve exact source/version and the prior DesignDelta, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A supplier has already shipped the old revision: decide disposition explicitly. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (decide disposition explicitly.) through the existing stage result for DesignDelta; preserve exact source/version and the prior DesignDelta, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A fielded unit is grandfathered: preserve its approved configuration and maintenance guidance. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve its approved configuration and maintenance guidance.) through the existing stage result for DesignDelta; preserve exact source/version and the prior DesignDelta, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A drawing reference changes numbering only: avoid unnecessary operational churn. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (avoid unnecessary operational churn.) through the existing stage result for DesignDelta; preserve exact source/version and the prior DesignDelta, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A retrofit is partially completed: track mixed-state constraints until verification. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (track mixed-state constraints until verification.) through the existing stage result for DesignDelta; preserve exact source/version and the prior DesignDelta, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretChange: interpretChangeResult, resolveApplicability: resolveApplicabilityResult, traceDependencies: traceDependenciesResult, planImplementation: planImplementationResult, verifyConfiguration: verifyConfigurationResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
